1. **A broadcast receiver comprising:**

a receiving circuit configured to receive a broadcast signal carrying audiovisual content, tag information synchronized with respective scenes of the audiovisual content, and an application information table;

a tag acquisition circuit configured to extract, from the broadcast signal, tag information corresponding to a scene being presented;

an application acquisition circuit configured to obtain an application identified by the application information table;

a processing circuit configured to execute the application; and

an information acquisition circuit configured to acquire, based on the extracted tag information, related program information associated with the scene being presented and to provide the related program information to the application.

1. A system for supplying content associated with a broadcast service to an executing application, the system comprising:  
a receiver configured to receive a broadcast signal carrying audiovisual program content, tag information associated with the audiovisual program content, and an application information table, the tag information including a tag identifier;  
a tag extractor configured to extract the tag information from the received broadcast signal and identify the tag identifier included in the extracted tag information;  
a memory configured to store at least a portion of the application information table, the application information table including, for each of a plurality of applications, an application identifier and content-association information that associates at least one tag identifier with content available to the respective application;  
a processor configured to execute an application identified by an application identifier included in the application information table and, in response to extraction of the tag information, determine that the identified tag identifier is associated with the executing application by comparing the identified tag identifier with the content-association information corresponding to the executing application in the application information table; and  
a content-supply module configured, responsive to the processor determining that the identified tag identifier is associated with the executing application, to identify associated content specified by the content-association information, obtain the associated content from at least one of the broadcast signal, a local storage device, or a network-accessible content source, and supply the associated content to the executing application through an application interface, such that the executing application processes or presents the associated content in temporal association with the audiovisual program content.
